6 &#8211; <span id="xdx_82B_z939UoYC4sZi">Plant, Property and Equipment</span></span></b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, Sans-Serif">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, Sans-Serif">Property,
plant and equipment are stated at cost. Depreciation of property, plant and equipment begins in the month when the asset is placed into
service and is provided using the straight-line method for financial reporting purposes at rates based on the estimated useful lives
of the assets. Estimated useful lives range from three to twenty years. Property, plant and equipment consist of the following:</span></p>

